#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:645
msgid "How access rules work"
msgstr "Fonctionnement des règles d'accès"

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:651
#. translators: 1: the singular space label, lowercase (e.g. space, group). 2: member label, plural, lowercase (e.g. "members").
#, php-format, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A rule lets more people in to this %1$s: anyone who matches it gets what it "
"grants, without being added to the %2$s list. Who else gets in is set by "
"the %1$s's visibility and join policy. Adding a role, capability, trust "
"level or membership rule to a Public %1$s switches it to Private, so that "
"the rule is what decides who gets in."
msgstr ""
"%1$s : une règle laisse entrer plus de monde. Toute personne qui y "
"correspond obtient ce qu'elle accorde, sans être ajoutée à la liste des "
"%2$s. Qui d'autre peut entrer dépend de la visibilité et de la règle "
"d'adhésion. Si la visibilité est publique, ajouter une règle de rôle, de "
"capacité, de niveau de confiance ou d'abonnement la passe en privé, afin "
"que la règle décide qui peut entrer."

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:659
#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:665
#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:669
#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:673
msgid "What the person can do"
msgstr "Ce que la personne peut faire"

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:665
#. translators: %s: the owner-configured noun (space, topic, reply, member or category), sometimes with a count such as "14 spaces".
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Lets matching people in to read and report. It takes nothing away from "
"people who already get in another way, such as %s on the roster."
msgstr ""
"Laisse entrer les personnes concernées pour lire et signaler. Cela n'enlève "
"rien à celles qui entrent déjà autrement, comme les personnes de la liste "
"(%s)."

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:669
msgid "Read, plus post, reply, vote and report. The usual choice for a paid plan."
msgstr ""
"Lecture, plus publication, réponse, vote et signalement. Le choix habituel "
"pour une offre payante."

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:673
#. translators: 1: topic label, plural, lowercase (e.g. "topics"). 2: member label, lowercase (e.g. "member").
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Participate, plus edit other people's content, close and pin %1$s for "
"people whose WordPress role already allows moderation. Offered only on WP "
"Role and Capability rules: for any other rule an ordinary %2$s would get "
"exactly Participate."
msgstr ""
"Participer, modifier le contenu des autres, fermer et épingler les %1$s "
"pour les personnes dont le rôle WordPress autorise déjà la modération. "
"Proposé uniquement pour les règles de rôle WP et de capacité : pour toute "
"autre règle, chaque %2$s ordinaire obtiendrait exactement Participation."

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:678
#. translators: 1: member label (e.g. "Member"). 2: member label, plural (e.g. "Members").
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%1$s lists show a matching role - Read is listed as Viewer, Participate and "
"Full as Member. To give one person a different role, change it on the %2$s "
"tab; that keeps it a visible, per-person decision rather than a side effect "
"of a rule."
msgstr ""
"Dans les listes, chaque %1$s affiche le rôle correspondant : Lecture "
"apparaît comme Lecteur, Participation et Complet comme Membre. Pour donner "
"un autre rôle à une personne, modifie-le dans l'onglet %2$s : cela reste "
"une décision visible, personne par personne, et non un effet secondaire "
"d'une règle."

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:681
msgid "A rule can never hand out moderation."
msgstr "Une règle ne peut jamais accorder la modération."

#: includes/admin/views/space-edit.php:685
#. translators: 1: topic label, plural, lowercase (e.g. "topics"). 2: the singular space label the site owner configured, lowercase (e.g. space, group). 3: product name shown in wp-admin (default "Jetonomy").
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Editing, closing or pinning other people's %1$s comes from the person's "
"WordPress role - set those under %3$s - Settings - Permissions. Ordinary "
"taking part is different: being admitted to any %2$s, by a rule or by the "
"roster, carries reading, posting, replying, voting and reporting on its "
"own. That holds for roles %3$s does not map, such as the ones a course or "
"membership plugin creates for its own members."
msgstr ""
